        "supported": true,
        "reason": "Canonical selection branches establish the outer disable guard, index overrides, second fighter-color priority, composite-before-common-table priority and optional direct overlay. Canonical ftCo_800C0658 returns embedded overlay storage. Register allocation reads material and preceding-expression occupancy; the helper replaces its temporary next link before uploading the alpha-derived RGB ratio. The document appropriately preserves integer arithmetic, exhaustion assertions and unresolved template layout."
      },
      {
        "index": 1,
        "supported": true,
        "reason": "The canonical void signature and nested x2223_b3/chk1 guards support at most one stage, not guaranteed emission. The allocator independently confirms that material and nullable expression-chain arguments reserve occupied registers."
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "supported": true,
        "reason": "Canonical traversal writes diffuse only through non-null material pointers, skips instance children, follows siblings and ascends until no parent remains. It neither clones objects nor saves an initial-root boundary, supporting the proper-root qualification."
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "supported": true,
        "reason": "The canonical Game & Watch load caller passes x4_GAMEWATCH_COLOR[x619_costume_id]. The callee provides instance-pruned in-place propagation. Deferring loaded bytes and named-color ordering is appropriate; neither citation establishes them."
